# How It Works

Every request follows the same optimized pipeline.

## 1. Context Collection

Headroom intercepts all incoming context, including:

- Prompts
- Tool outputs
- Conversation history
- Source code
- JSON responses
- Build logs
- RAG documents
- Images

---

## 2. Intelligent Routing

The **ContentRouter** identifies the content type and automatically selects the most suitable compression strategy.

| Content Type | Compression Engine |
|--------------|-------------------|
| JSON | SmartCrusher |
| Source Code | CodeCompressor |
| Plain Text | Kompress-v2 |
| Images | Image Compression |
| Mixed Content | Hybrid Pipeline |

No manual configuration is required.

---

## 3. Compression

Compression is applied only where it provides measurable value.

Rather than removing information indiscriminately, Headroom prioritizes preserving semantic meaning while eliminating redundancy.

Benefits include:

- Lower token usage
- Reduced API cost
- Faster requests
- Higher context capacity
- Improved provider cache utilization

---

## 4. Reversible Compression (CCR)

Original content is retained locally.

If additional detail is required, the model can retrieve the original data using the CCR retrieval mechanism without permanently increasing prompt size.

This enables aggressive compression while maintaining accuracy.

---

## 5. Model Inference

The optimized prompt is sent to the configured LLM provider.

Supported providers include:

- OpenAI
- Anthropic
- Azure OpenAI
- Amazon Bedrock
- Google Gemini
- OpenAI-compatible APIs

---

# Why the Pipeline Matters

Traditional AI workflows repeatedly transmit the same large context.

Headroom minimizes redundant information before every request, allowing models to focus on the information that matters most.

This approach improves:

- Cost efficiency
- Latency
- Context utilization
- Cache hit rates
- Multi-agent collaboration

without requiring changes to existing applications.

