# Corporate Networks and SSL Inspection

Some enterprise environments perform SSL inspection using internally managed Certificate Authorities (CAs).

If installation fails with certificate verification errors, install Rust before installing Headroom:

```bash
curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh
rustup default stable
```

Then reinstall:

```bash
pip install "headroom-ai[all]"
```

Windows users:

```powershell
winget install Rustlang.Rustup
rustup default stable
```

---

## Strict TLS Validation

If Python 3.13+ reports strict certificate validation errors, temporarily disable strict verification:

```bash
HEADROOM_TLS_STRICT=0 headroom proxy --port 8787
```

This relaxes strict certificate validation while preserving standard TLS verification.

Refer to the documentation before using this option in production environments.

